---
export const prerender = false;

import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteMap from '../../../components/territorio/SiteMap.astro';
import { localizedPath } from '../../../i18n/routing';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const markers = [
  {
    id: 'puesco',
    nombre: 'Puesco-Lanín / Winkulmapu',
    lat: -39.42,
    lng: -71.75,
    tipo: 'principal' as const,
    aporte: '17,000 ha under Governance Agreement (2024)',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Winkulmapu Governance Agreement"
  description="17,000 hectares of the Puesco sector under Mapuche-Pewenche co-management"
  locale={locale}
>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="container container--reading">
      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="kicker">Territory · Winkulmapu</p>
        <h1 class="page-header__title">Governance Agreement</h1>
        <p class="page-header__lead">
          A historic milestone: binding executive authority of Mapuche-Pewenche communities
          over 17,000 hectares of Villarrica National Park.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="container wink-map">
      <SiteMap markers={markers} locale={locale} zoom={11} height="min(40vh, 22rem)" />
    </div>

    <div class="container container--reading">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Mid-20th century, most <em>mawiza</em> (mountain forests) of Curarrehue became part of
          Villarrica National Park. Despite being peweñantu —ancestral Mapuche land inhabited by
          the Pewenche for millennia— the park was imposed without co-management.
        </p>
        <p>
          After decades of mobilization, in 2024 the <strong>Winkulmapu Indigenous Association</strong>
          signed a Governance Agreement with CONAF and the Ministry of National Assets to manage
          a 17,000-hectare subsection of Puesco. The agreement grants binding executive authority
          —including invasive species management, especially wild boar.
        </p>
        <p>
          It emerges in the context of the <strong>Biodiversity and Protected Areas Service (SBAP)</strong>
          and future «Indigenous Conservation Areas». Neither is fully operational yet: the Agreement
          sits at the frontier of an extraordinary policy transformation and is this Fondecyt’s
          primary (co)laboratory.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Mapuche <em>kintukafe</em> (researcher) formally participates in all four objectives
          representing Winkulmapu.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href={localizedPath('/territorio', locale)}>← Back to Territory</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .wink-map {
    margin-block: 0 var(--s-10);
  }
</style>
